Z||000062||Oreif||06-20-2001||11:45 AM||||So lets see a pic of your car? As for cracks in the roof and 17" wheels you are incorrect. The cracks probably came from the roof bolts/sunvisor bolts being overtightened at one point. This puts a lot of pressure on the A pillars and over normal driving on rough roads will cause cracks. Either that or someone swapped in the sunroof panel and was not careful. <BR>Your attitude about 2.5L's, DAD's car, and your general disposition makes it sound like the cars don't have a crack problem but I think everyone here knows who has the crack problem.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||1
