Z||000064||rogergarrison||06-20-2001||12:03 PM||||the only reason the 17'' rims ride any rougher is because you have to use lower profile tires. The lower the sidewall, the less area to absorb bumps. Most people with the low profile tires just slow down on speedbumps and such to keep from dragging bottoms across them. The wheels have nothing to do with your car getting cracks anywhere unless its to top of fender wells hitting tires. You cant make your car ride rough enough to crack the pillars even if you took out all the springs or put 200 pnds of air in the tires. If you give me a new set of 17'' rims Ill use them and if it causes any cracks anywhere on my car Ill give it to you with the title. And I dont baby my car either, I run it.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
