Z||000066||stimpy||06-20-2001||12:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>You don't think that STIMPY jumped over the fence and made ENEMIES do you?<BR>He must have really kicked some serious bootie!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, really, I would never stoop to using the kind of foul language. I'm very proud of my vocabulary. I gots mad wordz & I know how to use em.  So seriously, I do hope no-one thinks that I or my simple minded alter-ego Maniak84 is responsible for this booger-munching imbecile.<BR>And if anyone else is doing this Maniak style, time to back off, it's only mildly humorous at best.<P>If this nose picker is for real, lets hope the librarian pulls his internet privledges.  ||||reg||1
Z||000067||Slammed Fiero||06-20-2001||01:06 PM||||If you think about it , cracks resulting from rims and tires is pretty difficult. The fiero's body is bolted to the frame. None of the gaps really touch each other , they all have room to move a tiny amount with stress. You think if there was ANY real damage it would be to the spaceframe , the body panels have no structural merit , there just gravy on top.<P>My car is really stiff , it does creak , and I'm sure the stiff suspension will take it's toll on the door pins someday. But I don't think body damage is in the cards. <P>the interior pieces creak sometimes in and out of driveways , this is on a 40,000 mile car. I find my car handles and tracks better with the 17's than it did with the 15's and low profiles. Fiero's need lots of rubber outback to compensate for the weight. <P>JM <P>PS , if you can get into my geocities webpage , let me know , I haven't been able to get into it since yahoo bought geocities.||||reg||1
